     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">See below, thanks!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> Paolo De Marco &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">paolo....@iucs.cespu.pt</a>&gt;\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Sunday, August 12, 2018 8:05 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Levesque, Nicole M. &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">leve...@hsph.harvard.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> MaAsLin<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Dear Nicole,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I have a very quick doubt about a parameter description in MaAsLin: in &quot;</span><strong><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Minimum for feature prevalence filtering</span></strong><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> The\r\n minimum percentage of samples a feature can have abudance in before being removed.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">&quot; does the default value &quot;0.01&quot; really mean 0.01% or is it in fact 1% (0.01)?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I tried using the MaAsLin contact email (<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tti...@hsph.harvard.edu</a>) but it doesn&#39;t work any longer. I also tried emailing Dr. Huttenhower directly, but\r\n got no reply. Would you be able to help me??<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Thanks a lot. Best regards.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Paolo De Marco<br>\r\nProf. Auxiliar<br>\r\nIUCS, CESPU<br>\r\nGandra Paredes<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Portugal<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
